extraction_notes: |
  - Underseas, printed 60-61. The ley line walkers and sorcerers of the sea.
    The Experience Tables on printed 214 call the class "Ocean Mage" and the
    chapter heading calls it the "Ocean Wizard O.C.C."; the entry''s own first
    sentence says the two names mean the same thing, so the heading spelling is
    stored and the ladder spelling is recorded here.
  - ITS FIRST GRANTED SPELL IS NOT AN OCEAN SPELL. Printed 60 item 7 starts the
    wizard with "breathe without air", which is the CORE Rifts invocation and
    is in this catalog unprefixed - not `Ocean: Breathe Air`, which is a
    different spell in the ocean list, for a gilled creature to breathe AIR.
    The two read almost identically and mean opposite things. The core row is
    granted; the ocean row is not.
  - THE PER-LEVEL GRANT IS CAPPED AT THE CHARACTER''S OWN LEVEL. Printed 60 item
    7 gives one new spell per level "equal or below his own experience level",
    which is exactly `spells_per_level_levels: up_to_character_level` - the Ley
    Line Walker''s rule. The CREATION picks are capped at level five instead,
    which is a different cap and is in the starting group''s note, because a
    starting group has no level gate of its own.
  - HAND TO HAND COSTS DOUBLE HERE. Most classes in this book sell expert for
    one skill selection; this one charges two, and martial arts three. It is in
    the skill''s note; there is no key for the price of an upgrade.
  - NO `sdc_base` AND NO `mdc_base`, so it needs a `CORE_SDC_BY_CLASS` entry.
    1D6: a spell caster with Hand to Hand: Basic and no W.P. granted at all.
  - THE PILOT EXCLUSIONS NAME FIVE ROWS FOR FOUR WORDS, each checked against
    production first because an unmatched `except` fails OPEN. See the Whale
    Singer''s notes for the mapping.
