# Ocean Wizard

## Lore

Ocean wizards, also known as ocean mages, are fundamentally the ley line walkers and sorcerers of the sea. Many intelligent aquatic races - and a handful of humans and surface-dwelling D-bees living on islands, along coastlines, or near oceans and seas - have learned this water-specific mystic art.

Surface-dwelling ocean wizards, like air and water warlocks, are sought after by sailors, ship-line owners, sea merchants and businessmen: to protect vessels from danger, and for undersea salvage, exploration, mining, building and rescue work.

## GM Notes

The ocean wizard''s abilities are written for beings that are not cetaceans or pneuma-biforms - a whale singer or a biform gets its own versions.

Its magic is narrower than a whale singer''s in one direction and wider in another: no spellsongs and no dolphin magic at all, but a spell every level drawn from the whole ocean list, plus whatever it can find or buy under the Pursuit of Magic rules. A wizard with money and contacts can outrun its own experience level that way.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'ocean-wizard');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'ocean-wizard';
SELECT count(*) AS stub_gear FROM gear WHERE slug IN ('wet-suit', 'scuba-gear');

